1
00:00:00,250 --> 00:00:03,400
At the end of Part 1, the whole theory fit on one screen:

2
00:00:03,400 --> 00:00:07,212
the Schrödinger equation, the Born rule, and the commutator of position and

3
00:00:07,212 --> 00:00:08,250
momentum.

4
00:00:08,250 --> 00:00:10,125
But look at how we got them.

5
00:00:10,125 --> 00:00:13,325
We guessed the equation by making it work for plane waves.

6
00:00:13,325 --> 00:00:15,675
We took the Born rule as a postulate.

7
00:00:15,675 --> 00:00:19,300
And we computed the commutator from a formula for momentum that we had also

8
00:00:19,300 --> 00:00:20,238
guessed.

9
00:00:20,238 --> 00:00:25,275
In this video, we derive them, and then we put them to work.

10
00:00:25,708 --> 00:00:29,121
Start with the double slit again, seen Richard Feynman's way.

11
00:00:29,121 --> 00:00:31,746
A source on the left, two slits, a screen.

12
00:00:31,746 --> 00:00:34,958
Pick one point on the screen, and consider every way to get there:

13
00:00:34,958 --> 00:00:36,746
through any point of either slit.

14
00:00:36,746 --> 00:00:40,721
Each path contributes an arrow, and the arrow turns one full revolution for

15
00:00:40,721 --> 00:00:44,596
every wavelength of path length, so the color of each path shows which way

16
00:00:44,596 --> 00:00:46,083
its arrow points.

17
00:00:46,083 --> 00:00:49,058
Now add all the arrows, tip to tail.

18
00:00:49,058 --> 00:00:53,008
The paths through each slit give a gently curving string of arrows;

19
00:00:53,008 --> 00:00:54,696
the two strings join;

20
00:00:54,696 --> 00:00:59,058
and the length of the total, squared, is the brightness at that point.

21
00:00:59,058 --> 00:01:00,408
Now move the point.

22
00:01:00,408 --> 00:01:04,908
As it moves, the path lengths change, the arrows swing around, and the total

23
00:01:04,908 --> 00:01:06,546
grows and shrinks.

24
00:01:06,546 --> 00:01:10,771
Tracing its length squared along the screen draws the interference fringes.

25
00:01:10,771 --> 00:01:12,846
In Part 1 we had two arrows;

26
00:01:12,846 --> 00:01:16,596
here every point of each slit has its own, and the fringes come out with the

27
00:01:16,596 --> 00:01:19,267
slits' finite width built in.

28
00:01:19,267 --> 00:01:21,829
Feynman's real claim is far stronger:

29
00:01:21,829 --> 00:01:25,817
not just straight paths through the slits, but every path at all, however

30
00:01:25,817 --> 00:01:30,479
wild, contributes an arrow, turning at a rate set by a quantity from classical

31
00:01:30,479 --> 00:01:32,542
mechanics, the action.

32
00:01:32,542 --> 00:01:36,917
That single idea contains the Schrödinger equation, and it explains why a

33
00:01:36,917 --> 00:01:40,692
thrown ball follows just one path.

34
00:01:41,117 --> 00:01:43,092
It's one of three roads we'll take.

35
00:01:43,092 --> 00:01:44,542
The first is symmetry:

36
00:01:44,542 --> 00:01:48,629
the laws don't change from moment to moment, or from place to place, and those

37
00:01:48,629 --> 00:01:52,679
two facts alone force the Schrödinger equation and the commutator.

38
00:01:52,679 --> 00:01:55,529
The second is Feynman's sum over paths.

39
00:01:55,529 --> 00:01:59,992
The third runs backward from classical mechanics, and explains the old quantum

40
00:01:59,992 --> 00:02:02,204
rules of Bohr and Sommerfeld.

41
00:02:02,204 --> 00:02:05,892
All three arrive at the same theory.

42
00:02:06,342 --> 00:02:07,954
Then we'll use the theory.

43
00:02:07,954 --> 00:02:12,467
Approximation methods for real atoms, what identical particles do, from helium

44
00:02:12,467 --> 00:02:16,367
to the periodic table and solids, what happens to interference when a system

45
00:02:16,367 --> 00:02:20,642
touches its environment, and finally Dirac's equation, where relativity brings

46
00:02:20,642 --> 00:02:22,004
in antimatter.

47
00:02:22,004 --> 00:02:25,579
This is Part 2, and it's more mathematical than Part 1;

48
00:02:25,579 --> 00:02:29,842
it assumes the wavefunction, operators, commutators and the hydrogen atom

49
00:02:29,842 --> 00:02:30,829
from there.

50
00:02:30,829 --> 00:02:34,692
Every derivation is on screen, and every picture is computed.

51
00:02:36,873 --> 00:02:37,536
Part 1:

52
00:02:37,536 --> 00:02:39,823
Symmetry.

53
00:02:40,581 --> 00:02:43,181
What is a symmetry, in quantum mechanics?

54
00:02:43,181 --> 00:02:47,819
It's a change in how we describe things that leaves every prediction unchanged:

55
00:02:47,819 --> 00:02:51,831
turn your lab around, start your clock later, move everything a meter to the

56
00:02:51,831 --> 00:02:52,794
left.

57
00:02:52,794 --> 00:02:57,331
Every prediction is a probability, the squared size of an inner product, so

58
00:02:57,331 --> 00:03:01,356
a symmetry must preserve the size of every inner product.

59
00:03:01,356 --> 00:03:06,769
Eugene Wigner showed in 1931 that such a map can always be chosen to be unitary,

60
00:03:06,769 --> 00:03:12,256
U dagger U equals one, which preserves inner products exactly, or antiunitary,

61
00:03:12,256 --> 00:03:14,269
which also conjugates them;

62
00:03:14,269 --> 00:03:17,756
that second kind is needed only for time reversal.

63
00:03:17,756 --> 00:03:22,256
Geometrically, a unitary is a rigid rotation of Hilbert space:

64
00:03:22,256 --> 00:03:26,206
lengths and angles all stay the same.

65
00:03:26,423 --> 00:03:28,186
Now apply this to time.

66
00:03:28,186 --> 00:03:32,123
Let U of t take any state at time zero to the state at time t.

67
00:03:32,123 --> 00:03:36,861
If the laws are the same at every moment, evolving for s and then for t is

68
00:03:36,861 --> 00:03:39,598
the same as evolving for s plus t:

69
00:03:39,598 --> 00:03:46,023
U of t plus s equals U of t times U of s, with U of zero the identity.

70
00:03:46,023 --> 00:03:50,523
A family like this is called a one-parameter group, and Marshall Stone proved

71
00:03:50,523 --> 00:03:57,173
in 1932 that every continuous one has the form e to the minus i t H over h-bar,

72
00:03:57,173 --> 00:04:01,523
for a unique self-adjoint operator H.

73
00:04:01,973 --> 00:04:03,873
Here's the heart of that argument.

74
00:04:03,873 --> 00:04:07,936
For a tiny time epsilon, U is the identity plus something small:

75
00:04:07,936 --> 00:04:11,011
call it minus i epsilon H over h-bar.

76
00:04:11,011 --> 00:04:12,086
That defines H.

77
00:04:12,086 --> 00:04:13,948
Now demand unitarity.

78
00:04:13,948 --> 00:04:16,048
Multiply out U dagger U:

79
00:04:16,048 --> 00:04:21,148
the first-order term is i epsilon over h-bar times H dagger minus H, and it

80
00:04:21,148 --> 00:04:22,398
must vanish.

81
00:04:22,398 --> 00:04:24,486
So H equals its own adjoint:

82
00:04:24,486 --> 00:04:26,190
it's Hermitian.

83
00:04:26,190 --> 00:04:28,140
Now differentiate the group law:

84
00:04:28,140 --> 00:04:32,877
the change in U over a short time is U of epsilon minus one, over epsilon,

85
00:04:32,877 --> 00:04:33,765
times U of t.

86
00:04:33,765 --> 00:04:37,677
By the first line, that's minus i over h-bar, H, U.

87
00:04:37,677 --> 00:04:42,165
Act on any state, and you get i h-bar times the time derivative of psi equals

88
00:04:42,165 --> 00:04:43,452
H psi.

89
00:04:43,452 --> 00:04:46,402
The Schrödinger equation, with no waves anywhere:

90
00:04:46,402 --> 00:04:50,515
only the assumption that the laws don't change with time, and that probabilities

91
00:04:50,515 --> 00:04:53,040
are conserved.

92
00:04:53,548 --> 00:04:56,061
And the i is no longer mysterious.

93
00:04:56,061 --> 00:05:01,398
A unitary operator close to the identity is the identity plus a small anti-Hermitian

94
00:05:01,398 --> 00:05:02,461
operator;

95
00:05:02,461 --> 00:05:06,761
writing it as minus i times a Hermitian one is bookkeeping that makes H's

96
00:05:06,761 --> 00:05:08,461
eigenvalues real.

97
00:05:08,461 --> 00:05:10,461
You've seen the same thing in the plane:

98
00:05:10,461 --> 00:05:15,261
rotating a vector, its velocity is always perpendicular to it, and the matrix

99
00:05:15,261 --> 00:05:19,373
J that turns a vector a quarter turn squares to minus one.

100
00:05:19,373 --> 00:05:24,148
Exponentiate a generator like that, term by term, and the partial sums spiral

101
00:05:24,148 --> 00:05:25,411
onto the circle.

102
00:05:25,411 --> 00:05:28,523
Rotations come from an i.

103
00:05:29,373 --> 00:05:30,223
What is H?

104
00:05:30,223 --> 00:05:34,398
It's the generator of time translations, and it commutes with U, so its average

105
00:05:34,398 --> 00:05:35,761
never changes.

106
00:05:35,761 --> 00:05:40,311
That's what energy is, in quantum mechanics and in classical mechanics alike.

107
00:05:40,311 --> 00:05:44,036
The constant h-bar just converts the rate at which phases turn into units

108
00:05:44,036 --> 00:05:47,236
of energy, and its value comes from experiment.

109
00:05:47,236 --> 00:05:51,423
For an energy eigenstate the evolution is a single turning phase, e to the

110
00:05:51,423 --> 00:05:53,861
minus i E t over h-bar:

111
00:05:53,861 --> 00:05:55,648
Part 1's clocks.

112
00:05:55,648 --> 00:06:00,323
And for a spin in a magnetic field, U of t is a rigid rotation of the whole

113
00:06:00,323 --> 00:06:01,973
Bloch sphere about the field.

114
00:06:03,971 --> 00:06:05,784
Space works the same way.

115
00:06:05,784 --> 00:06:09,559
Let T of a be the operator that slides every wavefunction a distance a to

116
00:06:09,559 --> 00:06:10,521
the right:

117
00:06:10,521 --> 00:06:12,709
psi of x becomes psi of x minus a.

118
00:06:12,709 --> 00:06:17,071
Sliding twice adds the distances, and nothing about probabilities changes,

119
00:06:17,071 --> 00:06:22,484
so T is a one-parameter unitary group, and by Stone's theorem it has a generator.

120
00:06:22,484 --> 00:06:23,584
Call it P:

121
00:06:23,584 --> 00:06:27,384
T of a equals e to the minus i a P over h-bar.

122
00:06:27,384 --> 00:06:29,471
This is the definition of momentum:

123
00:06:29,471 --> 00:06:31,896
the generator of translations.

124
00:06:31,896 --> 00:06:36,721
If the Hamiltonian doesn't care where things are, H commutes with T, and momentum

125
00:06:36,721 --> 00:06:39,271
is conserved.

126
00:06:39,454 --> 00:06:43,742
Now we can derive the commutator, instead of computing it from a guess.

127
00:06:43,742 --> 00:06:48,817
A position eigenstate, slid by a, is the position eigenstate at x plus a.

128
00:06:48,817 --> 00:06:52,892
So measuring position after the slide gives x plus a, and before it gives

129
00:06:52,892 --> 00:06:53,817
x:

130
00:06:53,817 --> 00:06:57,179
X and T fail to commute, by exactly a times T.

131
00:06:57,179 --> 00:07:01,371
That's true for every x, so it's an operator equation.

132
00:07:01,371 --> 00:07:03,534
Expand T for a small slide:

133
00:07:03,534 --> 00:07:06,096
one minus i a P over h-bar.

134
00:07:06,096 --> 00:07:10,759
The identity commutes with everything, and what's left is minus i a over h-bar

135
00:07:10,759 --> 00:07:13,696
times X P minus P X, equal to a.

136
00:07:13,696 --> 00:07:15,084
Divide by a:

137
00:07:15,084 --> 00:07:18,409
X P minus P X equals i h-bar.

138
00:07:18,409 --> 00:07:22,571
The canonical commutation relation is just the statement that momentum moves

139
00:07:22,571 --> 00:07:24,946
position.

140
00:07:25,379 --> 00:07:27,717
And the formula for momentum follows.

141
00:07:27,717 --> 00:07:31,779
In the position basis, the slid wavefunction is psi of x minus a.

142
00:07:31,779 --> 00:07:34,542
Expand both sides to first order in a:

143
00:07:34,542 --> 00:07:38,229
Taylor's theorem on one side, the generator on the other.

144
00:07:38,229 --> 00:07:43,267
Matching them, P acting on psi is minus i h-bar times the derivative.

145
00:07:43,267 --> 00:07:44,604
Part 1 guessed this;

146
00:07:44,604 --> 00:07:47,129
here it's forced.

147
00:07:47,596 --> 00:07:49,746
One consequence is startling.

148
00:07:49,746 --> 00:07:55,196
No finite matrices can satisfy X P minus P X equals i h-bar.

149
00:07:55,196 --> 00:07:59,759
The trace of any commutator is zero, because the trace of X P equals the trace

150
00:07:59,759 --> 00:08:00,759
of P X.

151
00:08:00,759 --> 00:08:06,121
Here's a random five-by-five example, whose diagonal entries cancel exactly.

152
00:08:06,121 --> 00:08:11,896
But the trace of i h-bar times the identity is i h-bar times the dimension.

153
00:08:11,896 --> 00:08:16,446
So the Hilbert space of a particle on a line has to be infinite-dimensional,

154
00:08:16,446 --> 00:08:21,434
and, as Stone and von Neumann proved, any operators satisfying the relation

155
00:08:21,434 --> 00:08:26,084
are just x and minus i h-bar d d x in disguise.

156
00:08:26,084 --> 00:08:31,571
That's why Heisenberg's matrices and Schrödinger's waves had to agree.

157
00:08:32,029 --> 00:08:36,404
Boosts, changing to a frame moving at velocity v, give the rest.

158
00:08:36,404 --> 00:08:41,379
Seen from the moving frame, every momentum shifts by m v, and on a wavefunction

159
00:08:41,379 --> 00:08:45,892
that's multiplication by e to the i m v x over h-bar:

160
00:08:45,892 --> 00:08:49,729
a twist of the phase that winds the colors faster, while the density doesn't

161
00:08:49,729 --> 00:08:51,054
change at all.

162
00:08:51,054 --> 00:08:56,779
Watch the momentum distribution slide over by exactly m v.

163
00:08:56,921 --> 00:08:59,646
Now require that velocities add properly:

164
00:08:59,646 --> 00:09:03,996
the rate of change of X, which by the Heisenberg equation is i over h-bar

165
00:09:03,996 --> 00:09:09,059
times the commutator of H with X, must be P over m in every frame.

166
00:09:09,059 --> 00:09:14,434
The kinetic energy, P squared over 2m, has exactly that commutator with X.

167
00:09:14,434 --> 00:09:19,496
So H minus P squared over 2m commutes with X, and anything that commutes with

168
00:09:19,496 --> 00:09:22,396
position is a function of position.

169
00:09:22,396 --> 00:09:25,796
H equals P squared over 2m plus V of X.

170
00:09:25,796 --> 00:09:31,396
The form of the Hamiltonian, derived from Galilean relativity.

171
00:09:31,829 --> 00:09:34,692
One last detail will come back again and again.

172
00:09:34,692 --> 00:09:38,079
Slide by a and then boost, or boost and then slide:

173
00:09:38,079 --> 00:09:43,229
the results differ only by a phase, e to the minus i m v a over h-bar.

174
00:09:43,229 --> 00:09:48,479
And m v a is the area of a rectangle in phase space, a wide and m v tall.

175
00:09:48,479 --> 00:09:50,929
Phase equals area over h-bar.

176
00:09:50,929 --> 00:09:54,954
We'll meet it next with magnetic flux, and later in the old quantum rules.

177
00:09:57,002 --> 00:10:01,277
Rotations are the third symmetry, and the most interesting, because they don't

178
00:10:01,277 --> 00:10:02,265
commute.

179
00:10:02,265 --> 00:10:06,102
Turn a book a quarter turn about one axis and then about another;

180
00:10:06,102 --> 00:10:08,290
now do it in the opposite order.

181
00:10:08,290 --> 00:10:12,002
The book ends up facing a different way.

182
00:10:12,135 --> 00:10:13,873
Even for tiny turns:

183
00:10:13,873 --> 00:10:18,773
rotate by epsilon about x, then about y, then undo both, and you're left with

184
00:10:18,773 --> 00:10:21,960
a rotation about z by epsilon squared.

185
00:10:21,960 --> 00:10:25,210
Here are the numbers, for real rotation matrices:

186
00:10:25,210 --> 00:10:29,710
the leftover angle divided by epsilon squared goes to one, and its axis to

187
00:10:29,710 --> 00:10:31,960
z.

188
00:10:32,360 --> 00:10:37,510
Each rotation is a unitary, e to the minus i theta J over h-bar, and the three

189
00:10:37,510 --> 00:10:40,573
generators are the components of angular momentum.

190
00:10:40,573 --> 00:10:44,785
Expand that loop of four rotations to second order, match it to the leftover

191
00:10:44,785 --> 00:10:51,098
rotation about z, and you get J x J y minus J y J x equals i h-bar J z, and

192
00:10:51,098 --> 00:10:53,498
the same for every cyclic pair.

193
00:10:53,498 --> 00:10:58,610
That one algebraic relation determines every possible value of angular momentum,

194
00:10:58,610 --> 00:11:02,110
without solving any equation.

195
00:11:02,569 --> 00:11:03,456
Here's how.

196
00:11:03,456 --> 00:11:07,481
Combine J x and J y into J plus and J minus.

197
00:11:07,481 --> 00:11:12,656
Their commutator with J z is plus or minus h-bar times themselves, so J plus

198
00:11:12,656 --> 00:11:17,756
raises the z component by one unit of h-bar, and J minus lowers it.

199
00:11:17,756 --> 00:11:22,531
The total, J squared, commutes with all three components, so the whole ladder

200
00:11:22,531 --> 00:11:25,144
shares one value of J squared.

201
00:11:25,144 --> 00:11:29,519
But J z squared can't exceed J squared, so the ladder has a top rung, where

202
00:11:29,519 --> 00:11:32,306
J plus gives zero, and a bottom rung.

203
00:11:32,306 --> 00:11:37,031
Multiply out J minus J plus, apply it to the top rung, and J squared equals

204
00:11:37,031 --> 00:11:40,156
h-bar squared, j times j plus one.

205
00:11:40,156 --> 00:11:44,169
Do the same at the bottom with J plus J minus, and the bottom rung must be

206
00:11:44,169 --> 00:11:44,969
at minus j.

207
00:11:44,969 --> 00:11:49,594
Getting from minus j to j takes a whole number of steps, so two j is a whole

208
00:11:49,594 --> 00:11:51,744
number.

209
00:11:52,202 --> 00:11:56,465
So j can be zero, one, two, but also one half, three halves.

210
00:11:56,465 --> 00:12:01,465
Orbital angular momentum, x cross p, only gives whole numbers, because the

211
00:12:01,465 --> 00:12:06,065
phase e to the i m phi has to come back to itself after a full turn.

212
00:12:06,065 --> 00:12:09,802
The half-integers are spin, and the algebra allowed them before anyone knew

213
00:12:09,802 --> 00:12:10,990
they were needed:

214
00:12:10,990 --> 00:12:15,077
a rotation by three hundred sixty degrees multiplies such a state by minus

215
00:12:15,077 --> 00:12:19,802
one, the sign Part 1 found for the electron.

216
00:12:20,235 --> 00:12:24,110
Here's the ladder for j equals two, painted on spheres:

217
00:12:24,110 --> 00:12:28,810
the color is the phase of each spherical harmonic, the brightness its size.

218
00:12:28,810 --> 00:12:33,435
Going up, the phase winds once more around the vertical axis, and each step

219
00:12:33,435 --> 00:12:38,760
multiplies by exactly the square root of l times l plus one, minus m times

220
00:12:38,760 --> 00:12:43,910
m plus one, checked here on a grid to better than one part in ten thousand.

221
00:12:43,910 --> 00:12:49,560
And because J squared is j times j plus one, h-bar squared, while J z is at

222
00:12:49,560 --> 00:12:54,985
most j h-bar, angular momentum can never point exactly along an axis:

223
00:12:54,985 --> 00:12:57,810
the other two components can never both be zero.

224
00:12:59,841 --> 00:13:04,429
Part 1 showed that multiplying the whole wavefunction by one phase, e to the

225
00:13:04,429 --> 00:13:06,741
i alpha, changes nothing.

226
00:13:06,741 --> 00:13:08,779
So here's a bolder question.

227
00:13:08,779 --> 00:13:12,516
What if we change the phase by a different amount at every point?

228
00:13:12,516 --> 00:13:18,241
The colors scramble, but every probability stays exactly the same.

229
00:13:18,341 --> 00:13:21,279
The Schrödinger equation, however, notices.

230
00:13:21,279 --> 00:13:24,666
Apply the momentum operator to the new wavefunction.

231
00:13:24,666 --> 00:13:29,104
The product rule brings down an extra term, the gradient of the phase:

232
00:13:29,104 --> 00:13:33,229
as far as the equation is concerned, the particle has been given a momentum

233
00:13:33,229 --> 00:13:36,079
kick that varies from place to place.

234
00:13:36,079 --> 00:13:39,541
A pure change of bookkeeping would change the physics.

235
00:13:39,541 --> 00:13:42,016
There's only one way to rescue the symmetry.

236
00:13:42,016 --> 00:13:46,066
Introduce a field, A, that shifts by the same gradient whenever the phase

237
00:13:46,066 --> 00:13:49,529
is changed, and use p minus q A in place of p.

238
00:13:49,529 --> 00:13:52,129
Now the extra terms cancel exactly:

239
00:13:52,129 --> 00:13:56,429
p minus q A acting on the new wavefunction is just the phase factor times

240
00:13:56,429 --> 00:13:59,054
p minus q A acting on the old one.

241
00:13:59,054 --> 00:14:02,974
Do the same with time, and you need a second field, phi.

242
00:14:02,974 --> 00:14:08,337
The Hamiltonian becomes p minus q A, squared, over 2m, plus q phi:

243
00:14:08,337 --> 00:14:12,699
exactly how a charge couples to the electromagnetic potentials, with the electric

244
00:14:12,699 --> 00:14:17,074
and magnetic fields, built from derivatives of A and phi, unchanged by the

245
00:14:17,074 --> 00:14:18,537
phase change.

246
00:14:18,537 --> 00:14:23,537
Fock, London and Weyl found this between 1926 and 1929:

247
00:14:23,537 --> 00:14:29,924
demand that local phase changes be a symmetry, and electromagnetism appears.

248
00:14:30,366 --> 00:14:32,404
This has a startling consequence.

249
00:14:32,404 --> 00:14:37,191
A charged particle moving along a path picks up an extra phase, q over h-bar

250
00:14:37,191 --> 00:14:39,816
times the integral of A along the path.

251
00:14:39,816 --> 00:14:43,316
For two paths that start and end together, the difference is the integral

252
00:14:43,316 --> 00:14:47,216
around the loop, which by Stokes' theorem is the magnetic flux through the

253
00:14:47,216 --> 00:14:48,104
loop.

254
00:14:48,104 --> 00:14:53,104
So the relative phase is q times the flux, over h-bar, even if the magnetic

255
00:14:53,104 --> 00:14:56,291
field is zero everywhere the particle goes.

256
00:14:56,291 --> 00:14:58,966
Phase equals area over h-bar again;

257
00:14:58,966 --> 00:15:02,291
this time the area is threaded by magnetic flux.

258
00:15:02,291 --> 00:15:07,366
Aharonov and Bohm pointed this out in 1959.

259
00:15:07,799 --> 00:15:09,862
Here's the effect, simulated.

260
00:15:09,862 --> 00:15:12,599
An electron wave passes through two slits;

261
00:15:12,599 --> 00:15:16,799
hidden inside the wall between them is a thin tube of magnetic flux.

262
00:15:16,799 --> 00:15:18,424
The wave never reaches it:

263
00:15:18,424 --> 00:15:21,974
the density there stays below a ten-thousandth of its peak.

264
00:15:21,974 --> 00:15:23,924
On the left, no flux.

265
00:15:23,924 --> 00:15:27,962
On the right, half a flux quantum, and the bright central fringe has become

266
00:15:27,962 --> 00:15:30,449
a dark line.

267
00:15:30,683 --> 00:15:34,545
Now turn the flux up slowly, and watch the pattern on the screen.

268
00:15:34,545 --> 00:15:38,933
The fringes slide sideways under a fixed envelope, by one whole fringe for

269
00:15:38,933 --> 00:15:44,370
each flux quantum, h over e, and then the pattern is exactly what it was.

270
00:15:44,370 --> 00:15:48,633
The electrons never touch the magnetic field, yet they know how much flux

271
00:15:48,633 --> 00:15:51,208
they went around.

272
00:15:51,691 --> 00:15:57,204
In 1986 Akira Tonomura's group at Hitachi did it with electrons passing around

273
00:15:57,204 --> 00:16:02,141
a tiny ring-shaped magnet, sealed inside a superconductor so that no field

274
00:16:02,141 --> 00:16:03,479
could leak out.

275
00:16:03,479 --> 00:16:08,591
A superconducting ring traps flux only in multiples of h over 2e, half a flux

276
00:16:08,591 --> 00:16:13,529
quantum, so the fringes could only be shifted by zero or by half a fringe.

277
00:16:13,529 --> 00:16:15,316
That's exactly what they saw.

278
00:16:17,372 --> 00:16:18,085
Part 2:

279
00:16:18,085 --> 00:16:20,772
Sums over paths.

280
00:16:21,530 --> 00:16:24,980
Everything about time evolution is packed into one function:

281
00:16:24,980 --> 00:16:29,480
the amplitude to start at x a and be found at x b a time t later, called the

282
00:16:29,480 --> 00:16:30,768
propagator, K.

283
00:16:30,768 --> 00:16:34,930
Any initial wavefunction evolves by adding up the propagator from every starting

284
00:16:34,930 --> 00:16:35,918
point.

285
00:16:35,918 --> 00:16:39,643
For a free particle it's a Gaussian with an imaginary exponent:

286
00:16:39,643 --> 00:16:43,730
its size is the same everywhere, and its phase grows with the square of the

287
00:16:43,730 --> 00:16:47,830
distance, so the colors cycle faster and faster.

288
00:16:47,830 --> 00:16:53,530
A particle that starts at one point can be found anywhere a moment later.

289
00:16:53,689 --> 00:16:57,251
Feynman's way of thinking about K starts with the double slit.

290
00:16:57,251 --> 00:16:58,476
Add a third slit:

291
00:16:58,476 --> 00:16:59,726
three paths.

292
00:16:59,726 --> 00:17:01,989
Add a second screen with its own slits:

293
00:17:01,989 --> 00:17:05,076
the amplitude is a sum over every way through both.

294
00:17:05,076 --> 00:17:08,714
Keep adding screens and drilling holes, until there's nothing left of the

295
00:17:08,714 --> 00:17:09,889
screens.

296
00:17:09,889 --> 00:17:15,289
Now the amplitude is a sum over every path from source to detector.

297
00:17:15,730 --> 00:17:18,393
Here's the same idea as mathematics.

298
00:17:18,393 --> 00:17:22,705
Cut the time into N short steps of length epsilon, so the evolution is U of

299
00:17:22,705 --> 00:17:25,080
epsilon, applied N times.

300
00:17:25,080 --> 00:17:28,293
At each intermediate time, the particle could be anywhere:

301
00:17:28,293 --> 00:17:31,155
x 1, x 2, and so on.

302
00:17:31,155 --> 00:17:33,755
One choice of all of them is a zigzag path;

303
00:17:33,755 --> 00:17:37,255
every choice is a different zigzag.

304
00:17:37,755 --> 00:17:40,680
Write the propagator as N short evolutions.

305
00:17:40,680 --> 00:17:44,718
Between each pair of factors, insert a complete set of positions:

306
00:17:44,718 --> 00:17:48,418
one integral over x k for each intermediate time.

307
00:17:48,418 --> 00:17:52,455
For one short step, the propagator is the free one times a phase from the

308
00:17:52,455 --> 00:17:57,855
potential, and its exponent is i epsilon over h-bar times the kinetic minus

309
00:17:57,855 --> 00:17:59,430
the potential energy:

310
00:17:59,430 --> 00:18:01,255
the Lagrangian.

311
00:18:01,255 --> 00:18:05,843
Multiply N of these together and the exponents add up to i over h-bar times

312
00:18:05,843 --> 00:18:08,530
the action of the zigzag path through all the x k.

313
00:18:08,530 --> 00:18:12,418
Integrating over every x k means adding up every zigzag.

314
00:18:12,418 --> 00:18:17,968
In the limit, K is the integral over all paths of e to the i S over h-bar.

315
00:18:17,968 --> 00:18:23,780
Dirac noticed in 1933 that e to the i S over h-bar plays this role;

316
00:18:23,780 --> 00:18:29,655
Feynman, in 1948, showed it is all of quantum mechanics.

317
00:18:30,097 --> 00:18:31,960
Can we actually do this sum?

318
00:18:31,960 --> 00:18:36,597
In real time the arrows spin so fast that sampling paths is hopeless.

319
00:18:36,597 --> 00:18:41,097
But if we let time be imaginary, each path gets a positive weight, e to the

320
00:18:41,097 --> 00:18:45,672
minus the action, and the paths become Brownian motion, the subject of our

321
00:18:45,672 --> 00:18:47,885
stochastic calculus video.

322
00:18:47,885 --> 00:18:50,760
Then the sum is ordinary arithmetic.

323
00:18:50,760 --> 00:18:55,489
Here's the short-time kernel of the harmonic oscillator, as a matrix.

324
00:18:55,489 --> 00:18:57,951
Multiply it by itself again and again:

325
00:18:57,951 --> 00:19:02,189
any starting shape relaxes onto the ground state, the Gaussian, and the rate

326
00:19:02,189 --> 00:19:05,014
at which it shrinks gives the ground-state energy.

327
00:19:05,014 --> 00:19:09,401
With epsilon equal to one, the estimate is 0.481;

328
00:19:09,401 --> 00:19:14,051
at 0.05 it's 0.49995.

329
00:19:14,051 --> 00:19:19,564
The error falls like epsilon squared, toward exactly one half.

330
00:19:19,997 --> 00:19:22,260
Or sample the paths themselves.

331
00:19:22,260 --> 00:19:26,872
Here are closed random paths in imaginary time, each drawn with its proper

332
00:19:26,872 --> 00:19:29,885
weight, each with a hundred time slices.

333
00:19:29,885 --> 00:19:33,847
Histogram where they spend their time, and you get the ground-state density,

334
00:19:33,847 --> 00:19:36,447
computed from nothing but a sum over paths.

335
00:19:38,492 --> 00:19:42,305
Feynman's formulation has to agree with Schrödinger's, and checking that is

336
00:19:42,305 --> 00:19:44,455
a beautiful piece of calculus.

337
00:19:44,455 --> 00:19:47,742
Advance the wavefunction by one short step epsilon:

338
00:19:47,742 --> 00:19:52,205
integrate the short-time kernel against psi, over every displacement eta.

339
00:19:52,205 --> 00:19:56,355
The kernel's phase is m eta squared over two h-bar epsilon.

340
00:19:56,355 --> 00:20:00,867
Outside a window of width about the square root of h-bar epsilon over m, it

341
00:20:00,867 --> 00:20:04,567
oscillates so fast that its contributions cancel.

342
00:20:04,567 --> 00:20:09,455
As epsilon shrinks, the window shrinks, but only like the square root of epsilon.

343
00:20:09,455 --> 00:20:12,992
That square root is the whole story.

344
00:20:13,126 --> 00:20:16,301
Expand psi of x plus eta in a Taylor series.

345
00:20:16,301 --> 00:20:20,413
Normally we'd keep only the first-order term, but here eta squared is as big

346
00:20:20,413 --> 00:20:23,701
as epsilon, so the second derivative stays in.

347
00:20:23,701 --> 00:20:26,076
Now we need three Gaussian integrals.

348
00:20:26,076 --> 00:20:29,638
The kernel's normalization makes the first one exactly one.

349
00:20:29,638 --> 00:20:31,976
The second vanishes by symmetry.

350
00:20:31,976 --> 00:20:36,926
And the third, the average of eta squared, is i h-bar epsilon over m:

351
00:20:36,926 --> 00:20:39,692
the spread of the step, with an i in it.

352
00:20:39,692 --> 00:20:42,417
Collect everything to first order in epsilon.

353
00:20:42,417 --> 00:20:45,842
On the left, psi plus epsilon times its time derivative;

354
00:20:45,842 --> 00:20:50,317
on the right, the potential's phase times psi plus i h-bar epsilon over 2m

355
00:20:50,317 --> 00:20:52,117
times psi double prime.

356
00:20:52,117 --> 00:20:53,880
The psi terms cancel.

357
00:20:53,880 --> 00:20:58,367
Multiply by i h-bar over epsilon, and out comes the Schrödinger equation,

358
00:20:58,367 --> 00:20:59,942
every factor in place:

359
00:20:59,942 --> 00:21:03,892
the i, the h-bar squared over 2m, and the potential.

360
00:21:03,892 --> 00:21:08,867
Feynman did exactly this in his 1948 paper.

361
00:21:09,301 --> 00:21:12,688
That i h-bar epsilon over m deserves a second look.

362
00:21:12,688 --> 00:21:16,376
A step of size eta, whose square is proportional to the time step:

363
00:21:16,376 --> 00:21:20,576
it's the same rule as d W squared equals d t, the heart of the stochastic

364
00:21:20,576 --> 00:21:22,613
calculus video, just with an i.

365
00:21:22,613 --> 00:21:26,863
It means the paths that matter in Feynman's sum are not smooth curves at all.

366
00:21:26,863 --> 00:21:31,301
Here is a typical path, in imaginary time, at four zoom levels, each eight

367
00:21:31,301 --> 00:21:32,488
times closer:

368
00:21:32,488 --> 00:21:34,151
it never smooths out.

369
00:21:34,151 --> 00:21:39,401
The kinetic term in the Schrödinger equation is the trace of that roughness.

370
00:21:39,834 --> 00:21:42,084
The time-slicing isn't just a proof device;

371
00:21:42,084 --> 00:21:43,384
it's an algorithm.

372
00:21:43,384 --> 00:21:47,109
Split each short step into half a step of potential phase, the free kernel,

373
00:21:47,109 --> 00:21:49,184
and another half step of potential.

374
00:21:49,184 --> 00:21:53,384
The free kernel is just multiplication in momentum space, one fast Fourier

375
00:21:53,384 --> 00:21:54,796
transform away.

376
00:21:54,796 --> 00:21:57,921
That's how every simulation in Part 1 was computed.

377
00:21:57,921 --> 00:22:02,784
Here's a wave packet in an anharmonic well, evolved with fewer and fewer slices,

378
00:22:02,784 --> 00:22:04,734
compared with the exact answer:

379
00:22:04,734 --> 00:22:07,109
the error falls like epsilon squared.

380
00:22:09,074 --> 00:22:13,087
If every path counts, why does a thrown ball follow just one?

381
00:22:13,087 --> 00:22:16,649
Take a ball thrown straight up and caught again two seconds later.

382
00:22:16,649 --> 00:22:19,499
The classical path is a parabola in time.

383
00:22:19,499 --> 00:22:24,099
Now consider a whole family of other paths with the same start and end, bent

384
00:22:24,099 --> 00:22:26,291
by different amounts a.

385
00:22:26,291 --> 00:22:30,116
For each one, compute the action, the integral of kinetic minus potential

386
00:22:30,116 --> 00:22:31,103
energy.

387
00:22:31,103 --> 00:22:34,891
Plotted against a, it's a parabola, smallest at a equals zero:

388
00:22:34,891 --> 00:22:36,328
the classical path.

389
00:22:36,328 --> 00:22:40,441
Each path's arrow turns by S over h-bar, and that's its color.

390
00:22:40,441 --> 00:22:44,603
Near the bottom, neighboring paths have almost the same action, so their arrows

391
00:22:44,603 --> 00:22:46,141
point the same way.

392
00:22:46,141 --> 00:22:51,366
Far from it, the action changes quickly, and their arrows spin.

393
00:22:51,716 --> 00:22:54,366
Add the arrows tip to tail, in order of a.

394
00:22:54,366 --> 00:22:58,566
The middle of the chain, from paths near the classical one, is a long straight

395
00:22:58,566 --> 00:22:59,478
run.

396
00:22:59,478 --> 00:23:02,628
The ends curl into tight spirals that go nowhere:

397
00:23:02,628 --> 00:23:04,991
those paths cancel each other out.

398
00:23:04,991 --> 00:23:09,378
This curve is a Cornu spiral, the same one that describes light at the edge

399
00:23:09,378 --> 00:23:11,766
of a shadow.

400
00:23:11,974 --> 00:23:13,924
Now make h-bar smaller.

401
00:23:13,924 --> 00:23:18,274
The spirals wind tighter, the straight run shrinks, and fewer and fewer paths

402
00:23:18,274 --> 00:23:21,674
around the classical one survive.

403
00:23:22,099 --> 00:23:26,487
With two ways to bend the path, the picture is a whole plane of arrows.

404
00:23:26,487 --> 00:23:29,299
Color each point by its arrow's direction:

405
00:23:29,299 --> 00:23:33,099
the rings crowd together everywhere except at the center, where the action

406
00:23:33,099 --> 00:23:34,437
is stationary.

407
00:23:34,437 --> 00:23:38,324
That's the principle of stationary phase.

408
00:23:38,758 --> 00:23:42,483
So the paths that survive are those where small changes don't change the action,

409
00:23:42,483 --> 00:23:43,833
to first order.

410
00:23:43,833 --> 00:23:47,008
Vary the path by delta x, keeping its ends fixed.

411
00:23:47,008 --> 00:23:50,908
Integrate by parts, and the first-order change in S is the integral of delta

412
00:23:50,908 --> 00:23:52,458
x times something.

413
00:23:52,458 --> 00:23:56,458
For that to vanish for every delta x, the something must be zero:

414
00:23:56,458 --> 00:23:58,570
the Euler-Lagrange equation.

415
00:23:58,570 --> 00:24:03,895
For L equals one half m x dot squared minus V, it's m x double dot equals

416
00:24:03,895 --> 00:24:05,658
minus V prime.

417
00:24:05,658 --> 00:24:11,108
Newton's second law, recovered as the limit of quantum mechanics.

418
00:24:11,558 --> 00:24:13,758
How small is h-bar, really?

419
00:24:13,758 --> 00:24:17,658
For a one-gram ball moving at a meter per second for one second, the action

420
00:24:17,658 --> 00:24:21,295
is about four point seven times ten to the thirty h-bars:

421
00:24:21,295 --> 00:24:25,220
bending its path by the width of a single atom turns its arrow some forty

422
00:24:25,220 --> 00:24:26,670
billion times.

423
00:24:26,670 --> 00:24:28,983
Only the classical path survives.

424
00:24:28,983 --> 00:24:33,370
For an electron in an atom, the action around an orbit is about h itself;

425
00:24:33,370 --> 00:24:36,983
many paths contribute, and the world is quantum.

426
00:24:36,983 --> 00:24:40,283
Fermat's principle for light rays is the same story:

427
00:24:40,283 --> 00:24:43,083
rays are where the phases of waves are stationary.

428
00:24:45,097 --> 00:24:48,810
The third road runs backward, from classical mechanics.

429
00:24:48,810 --> 00:24:52,760
Look for solutions with a classical-looking action in the exponent:

430
00:24:52,760 --> 00:24:57,772
an amplitude A times e to the i S over h-bar, both functions of x.

431
00:24:57,772 --> 00:25:01,797
Put that into the time-independent Schrödinger equation, and sort the terms

432
00:25:01,797 --> 00:25:04,131
by powers of h-bar.

433
00:25:04,131 --> 00:25:06,318
At order h-bar to the zero:

434
00:25:06,318 --> 00:25:09,206
S prime squared over 2m plus V equals E.

435
00:25:09,206 --> 00:25:12,843
That's the Hamilton-Jacobi equation of classical mechanics:

436
00:25:12,843 --> 00:25:17,743
S prime is the classical momentum, p of x, and the phase is the integral of

437
00:25:17,743 --> 00:25:18,056
p.

438
00:25:18,056 --> 00:25:23,031
At the next order, two A prime S prime plus A S double prime equals zero,

439
00:25:23,031 --> 00:25:26,306
which says A squared times p is constant:

440
00:25:26,306 --> 00:25:28,843
A goes like one over the square root of p.

441
00:25:28,843 --> 00:25:33,381
Where the particle is slow, it's more likely to be found, just as a classical

442
00:25:33,381 --> 00:25:36,406
particle spends more time where it's slow.

443
00:25:36,406 --> 00:25:41,831
Dropping the next order is the WKB approximation, after Wentzel, Kramers and

444
00:25:41,831 --> 00:25:47,031
Brillouin in 1926, and Jeffreys before them.

445
00:25:47,489 --> 00:25:51,351
Here's how well it works, for a particle in a quartic well, V equals x to

446
00:25:51,351 --> 00:25:52,364
the fourth.

447
00:25:52,364 --> 00:25:57,076
The exact sixth state, computed numerically, and the WKB wave:

448
00:25:57,076 --> 00:26:00,926
inside the well they're nearly indistinguishable, with short wavelengths where

449
00:26:00,926 --> 00:26:04,464
the particle is fast, and big amplitudes where it's slow.

450
00:26:04,464 --> 00:26:08,464
But at the turning points, where p goes to zero, one over the square root

451
00:26:08,464 --> 00:26:11,164
of p blows up.

452
00:26:11,647 --> 00:26:15,597
Near a turning point the potential is nearly a straight line, and the exact

453
00:26:15,597 --> 00:26:18,147
solution there is an Airy function.

454
00:26:18,147 --> 00:26:23,097
Matching it to the WKB wave shows that each turning point shifts the phase

455
00:26:23,097 --> 00:26:26,322
by pi over four, an eighth of a cycle.

456
00:26:26,322 --> 00:26:30,122
So fitting a standing wave between two turning points requires the integral

457
00:26:30,122 --> 00:26:34,922
of p dx, there and back, to be n plus one half, times h.

458
00:26:34,922 --> 00:26:38,947
That's Bohr and Sommerfeld's quantum condition, with the half that Kramers

459
00:26:38,947 --> 00:26:41,097
found in 1926:

460
00:26:41,097 --> 00:26:47,047
his paper's title is "wave mechanics and half-integer quantization."

461
00:26:47,464 --> 00:26:48,189
The test:

462
00:26:48,189 --> 00:26:50,564
exact energies against this rule.

463
00:26:50,564 --> 00:26:53,251
The ground state is off by eighteen percent:

464
00:26:53,251 --> 00:26:56,614
it has barely one bump, hardly a short wavelength.

465
00:26:56,614 --> 00:27:00,676
But by the tenth state the error is three parts in ten thousand, and by the

466
00:27:00,676 --> 00:27:03,701
twentieth it's less than one in ten thousand.

467
00:27:03,701 --> 00:27:08,639
The old rule, without the half, is wrong at every n.

468
00:27:09,056 --> 00:27:10,793
And here's the geometry.

469
00:27:10,793 --> 00:27:14,918
Each energy level is a closed orbit in phase space, and the orbit for level

470
00:27:14,918 --> 00:27:18,206
n encloses an area of n plus one half times h.

471
00:27:18,206 --> 00:27:22,143
Consecutive orbits are separated by exactly one h of area:

472
00:27:22,143 --> 00:27:24,931
each quantum state occupies one cell of size h.

473
00:27:24,931 --> 00:27:28,681
Phase equals area over h-bar, one more time.

474
00:27:28,681 --> 00:27:32,968
And the Wigner function of the eighth state, computed from the exact wavefunction,

475
00:27:32,968 --> 00:27:37,431
lies right along its classical orbit, with interference ripples inside.

476
00:27:39,512 --> 00:27:44,325
WKB's formula for tunneling solved one of the great puzzles of the 1920s.

477
00:27:44,325 --> 00:27:49,587
Uranium-238 emits alpha particles with about 4.27 million electron volts of

478
00:27:49,587 --> 00:27:53,225
energy, and has a half-life of four and a half billion years.

479
00:27:53,225 --> 00:27:58,550
Polonium-212 emits them with 8.95, and lasts a third of a microsecond.

480
00:27:58,550 --> 00:28:02,112
Twice the energy, ten to the twenty-four times faster.

481
00:28:02,112 --> 00:28:05,300
Geiger and Nuttall had found the pattern in 1911;

482
00:28:05,300 --> 00:28:08,312
nobody could explain it.

483
00:28:08,754 --> 00:28:13,904
In 1928, George Gamow, and independently Ronald Gurney and Edward Condon,

484
00:28:13,904 --> 00:28:18,266
pictured the alpha particle rattling around inside the nucleus, held in by

485
00:28:18,266 --> 00:28:22,241
the electric repulsion of the rest of the nucleus once it's outside.

486
00:28:22,241 --> 00:28:26,241
The repulsion makes a barrier about twenty-eight million electron volts high

487
00:28:26,241 --> 00:28:29,991
at the nuclear surface, far above the alpha's energy.

488
00:28:29,991 --> 00:28:34,304
Classically it could only escape beyond sixty femtometers, and it could never

489
00:28:34,304 --> 00:28:36,529
get there.

490
00:28:36,962 --> 00:28:41,550
Quantum mechanically, it tunnels, and WKB gives the probability:

491
00:28:41,550 --> 00:28:45,387
e to the minus two times the integral of kappa across the forbidden region,

492
00:28:45,387 --> 00:28:50,425
where kappa is the square root of 2 mu times V minus Q, over h-bar.

493
00:28:50,425 --> 00:28:54,325
For a Coulomb barrier the integral can be done in closed form.

494
00:28:54,325 --> 00:28:57,075
For uranium the exponent is 88:

495
00:28:57,075 --> 00:29:00,900
each time the alpha hits the wall, it gets through with a probability of about

496
00:29:00,900 --> 00:29:03,187
one in ten to the thirty-eight.

497
00:29:03,187 --> 00:29:06,862
It hits the wall nearly ten to the twenty-one times a second, so it takes

498
00:29:06,862 --> 00:29:08,550
billions of years.

499
00:29:08,550 --> 00:29:13,812
For polonium-212, with twice the energy, the barrier is thinner, the exponent

500
00:29:13,812 --> 00:29:19,662
drops to 32, and the decay takes a fraction of a microsecond.

501
00:29:20,121 --> 00:29:24,696
Here are 29 alpha emitters, their half-lives from the nuclear data tables

502
00:29:24,696 --> 00:29:28,946
spanning twenty-four orders of magnitude, plotted against the nuclear charge

503
00:29:28,946 --> 00:29:31,208
over the square root of the energy.

504
00:29:31,208 --> 00:29:36,271
The crosses are Gamow's formula, with one assumed nuclear radius and no fitting

505
00:29:36,271 --> 00:29:37,546
to these data.

506
00:29:37,546 --> 00:29:41,333
It follows the measurements across all twenty-four decades, typically within

507
00:29:41,333 --> 00:29:43,021
a factor of two.

508
00:29:43,021 --> 00:29:49,846
The worst misses, polonium-210 and 208, sit at a closed shell of 126 neutrons,

509
00:29:49,846 --> 00:29:53,546
where forming an alpha particle inside the nucleus is harder:

510
00:29:53,546 --> 00:29:56,121
physics this simple picture leaves out.

511
00:29:56,121 --> 00:30:00,721
One integral, from the semiclassical limit of the Schrödinger equation, explains

512
00:30:00,721 --> 00:30:01,521
the rest.

513
00:30:03,528 --> 00:30:04,203
Part 3:

514
00:30:04,203 --> 00:30:06,878
Approximations.

515
00:30:07,594 --> 00:30:11,732
The box, the oscillator and hydrogen are almost the only systems we can solve

516
00:30:11,732 --> 00:30:12,857
exactly.

517
00:30:12,857 --> 00:30:16,982
Add a second electron, an electric field, or a slightly different shape, and

518
00:30:16,982 --> 00:30:18,944
exact solutions vanish.

519
00:30:18,944 --> 00:30:22,807
So most of quantum mechanics is approximation, done carefully.

520
00:30:22,807 --> 00:30:24,994
The workhorse is perturbation theory:

521
00:30:24,994 --> 00:30:29,794
split the Hamiltonian into a part we can solve, H zero, plus a small extra

522
00:30:29,794 --> 00:30:32,919
piece, lambda V.

523
00:30:33,319 --> 00:30:37,432
Expand both the energy and the state in powers of lambda, put them into the

524
00:30:37,432 --> 00:30:40,532
eigenvalue equation, and match powers.

525
00:30:40,532 --> 00:30:44,444
At first order, take the inner product with the unperturbed state.

526
00:30:44,444 --> 00:30:49,294
Because H zero is Hermitian, its terms cancel, and the first-order energy

527
00:30:49,294 --> 00:30:53,519
shift is simply the average of V in the unperturbed state.

528
00:30:53,519 --> 00:30:57,757
Taking the inner product with any other state m gives the first-order change

529
00:30:57,757 --> 00:30:58,869
of the state:

530
00:30:58,869 --> 00:31:02,669
V's matrix element, divided by the energy difference.

531
00:31:02,669 --> 00:31:07,132
And at second order, the energy shift is a sum of squared matrix elements

532
00:31:07,132 --> 00:31:09,094
over energy differences.

533
00:31:09,094 --> 00:31:13,544
For the ground state every denominator is negative, so second order always

534
00:31:13,544 --> 00:31:16,769
pushes the ground state down.

535
00:31:17,219 --> 00:31:20,307
Try it on a particle in a box, in a uniform field F.

536
00:31:20,307 --> 00:31:22,219
The first-order shift is zero:

537
00:31:22,219 --> 00:31:26,269
by symmetry, the average of x minus L over two vanishes.

538
00:31:26,269 --> 00:31:29,232
The second-order sum can be done in closed form:

539
00:31:29,232 --> 00:31:33,769
minus fifteen minus pi squared, over twenty-four pi to the fourth, times F

540
00:31:33,769 --> 00:31:34,757
squared.

541
00:31:34,757 --> 00:31:39,507
The computed sum agrees to six digits, and the exact energy follows the parabola

542
00:31:39,507 --> 00:31:44,219
at small fields, before higher orders take over.

543
00:31:44,728 --> 00:31:47,928
Notice the energy differences in the denominators:

544
00:31:47,928 --> 00:31:51,328
when two levels come close, they push each other apart.

545
00:31:51,328 --> 00:31:53,128
For two levels it's exact:

546
00:31:53,128 --> 00:31:59,328
the eigenvalues are hyperbolas, and the closest approach is twice the coupling.

547
00:31:59,786 --> 00:32:03,623
Here's a rectangular drum of fixed area, stretched one way and squeezed the

548
00:32:03,623 --> 00:32:04,411
other.

549
00:32:04,411 --> 00:32:08,736
Its levels cross freely, because the problem separates into x and y:

550
00:32:08,736 --> 00:32:11,748
states with different symmetries don't talk to each other.

551
00:32:11,748 --> 00:32:15,398
Add a small dent off-center, and the symmetry is gone.

552
00:32:15,398 --> 00:32:17,673
Every crossing opens up into a gap:

553
00:32:17,673 --> 00:32:20,461
levels of the same symmetry never cross.

554
00:32:20,461 --> 00:32:25,211
Wigner and von Neumann proved this in 1929.

555
00:32:25,711 --> 00:32:27,161
Last, a warning.

556
00:32:27,161 --> 00:32:31,048
For the anharmonic oscillator, the energy as a series in the coupling g can

557
00:32:31,048 --> 00:32:33,598
be computed exactly, to any order:

558
00:32:33,598 --> 00:32:38,661
one half, plus three quarters g, minus twenty-one eighths g squared, and on.

559
00:32:38,661 --> 00:32:41,498
But the coefficients grow like n factorial.

560
00:32:41,498 --> 00:32:45,073
The series converges for no value of g except zero:

561
00:32:45,073 --> 00:32:48,636
Bender and Wu proved it in 1969.

562
00:32:48,636 --> 00:32:49,948
Dyson saw why:

563
00:32:49,948 --> 00:32:52,586
flip the sign of g and the well opens up;

564
00:32:52,586 --> 00:32:57,494
the particle can tunnel out, and no smooth formula can cover both signs.

565
00:32:57,494 --> 00:33:01,269
Yet the partial sums are wonderfully accurate if you stop in time.

566
00:33:01,269 --> 00:33:06,569
At g equals 0.02, the error falls to three parts in a hundred million at order

567
00:33:06,569 --> 00:33:09,419
sixteen, then grows without bound.

568
00:33:09,419 --> 00:33:14,132
At g equals 0.05, the best you can do is order six.

569
00:33:14,132 --> 00:33:16,544
Perturbation series are asymptotic:

570
00:33:16,544 --> 00:33:19,094
use them, but stop at the smallest term.

571
00:33:21,142 --> 00:33:22,504
So far, energies.

572
00:33:22,504 --> 00:33:23,454
Now rates:

573
00:33:23,454 --> 00:33:25,329
how fast do things happen?

574
00:33:25,329 --> 00:33:28,779
Let a perturbation V act on a system that starts in state i.

575
00:33:28,779 --> 00:33:33,217
Write the state as a sum over energy eigenstates, with each one's clock factored

576
00:33:33,217 --> 00:33:34,079
out.

577
00:33:34,079 --> 00:33:38,692
The exact equations for the coefficients involve V's matrix elements, times

578
00:33:38,692 --> 00:33:41,179
phases turning at the Bohr frequencies.

579
00:33:41,179 --> 00:33:45,179
To first order, the amplitude to have jumped to state f is an integral of

580
00:33:45,179 --> 00:33:47,750
V times that turning phase.

581
00:33:47,750 --> 00:33:52,075
For a perturbation switched on at time zero and then held fixed, the integral

582
00:33:52,075 --> 00:33:57,475
is elementary, and the probability is V's matrix element squared, over h-bar

583
00:33:57,475 --> 00:34:02,475
squared, times this function of the detuning, omega.

584
00:34:02,917 --> 00:34:05,329
This function controls everything.

585
00:34:05,329 --> 00:34:10,092
As time goes on, its peak grows like t squared, while its width shrinks like

586
00:34:10,092 --> 00:34:11,079
one over t.

587
00:34:11,079 --> 00:34:16,267
So its area grows exactly like t, and the function concentrates into a spike:

588
00:34:16,267 --> 00:34:20,292
two pi t times a delta function.

589
00:34:20,425 --> 00:34:23,475
If there's just one final state, that means nothing much:

590
00:34:23,475 --> 00:34:25,950
the probability sloshes back and forth.

591
00:34:25,950 --> 00:34:30,137
But if the final states form a continuum, with rho states per unit energy,

592
00:34:30,137 --> 00:34:33,800
adding up the spike over all of them gives a probability that grows in proportion

593
00:34:33,800 --> 00:34:34,562
to t:

594
00:34:34,562 --> 00:34:36,050
a constant rate.

595
00:34:36,050 --> 00:34:41,575
Gamma equals two pi over h-bar, times V squared, times the density of states.

596
00:34:41,575 --> 00:34:44,137
Dirac derived it in 1927;

597
00:34:44,137 --> 00:34:47,625
Fermi called it the golden rule.

598
00:34:48,083 --> 00:34:49,933
Let's test it, exactly.

599
00:34:49,933 --> 00:34:55,196
One level, coupled with the same strength to 601 evenly spaced levels.

600
00:34:55,196 --> 00:34:59,246
Solve the Schrödinger equation exactly, and watch the probability of staying

601
00:34:59,246 --> 00:35:01,808
put, on a logarithmic scale.

602
00:35:01,808 --> 00:35:07,142
It falls off exponentially, at a rate within one percent of the golden rule's.

603
00:35:07,142 --> 00:35:12,342
Then, at two pi h-bar over the level spacing, every phase lines up again,

604
00:35:12,342 --> 00:35:14,479
and the probability comes back.

605
00:35:14,479 --> 00:35:17,854
A finite ladder of levels is not a true continuum;

606
00:35:17,854 --> 00:35:22,092
it only acts like one for times shorter than that.

607
00:35:22,525 --> 00:35:25,787
And the energy of whatever was emitted is spread out.

608
00:35:25,787 --> 00:35:29,637
Here are the populations of the 601 levels after the decay:

609
00:35:29,637 --> 00:35:34,037
a Lorentzian line whose full width is exactly h-bar gamma.

610
00:35:34,037 --> 00:35:38,000
A short lifetime means a broad line.

611
00:35:38,475 --> 00:35:42,562
In an atom, the continuum is the electromagnetic field itself.

612
00:35:42,562 --> 00:35:46,750
An excited hydrogen atom in its 2p state is coupled to the vacuum's photon

613
00:35:46,750 --> 00:35:50,337
modes, whose density grows like the frequency squared.

614
00:35:50,337 --> 00:35:54,075
Put in the dipole matrix element, and the golden rule gives a lifetime of

615
00:35:54,075 --> 00:35:58,137
1.596 nanoseconds, matching measurement.

616
00:35:58,137 --> 00:36:02,950
In that time the electron cloud sloshes about four million times, at the Lyman-alpha

617
00:36:02,950 --> 00:36:05,175
frequency, before the light gets out.

618
00:36:07,189 --> 00:36:07,864
Part 4:

619
00:36:07,864 --> 00:36:10,414
Many particles.

620
00:36:11,147 --> 00:36:15,197
Two particles share one wavefunction on the plane of their positions, x one

621
00:36:15,197 --> 00:36:17,572
and x two, as in Part 1.

622
00:36:17,572 --> 00:36:21,847
If the particles are identical, two electrons say, swapping them can't change

623
00:36:21,847 --> 00:36:23,122
any prediction.

624
00:36:23,122 --> 00:36:26,622
And swapping is reflecting the picture across the diagonal.

625
00:36:26,622 --> 00:36:31,485
So the swap, P, is a symmetry, and since swapping twice does nothing, P squared

626
00:36:31,485 --> 00:36:32,410
is one:

627
00:36:32,410 --> 00:36:36,881
its only possible eigenvalues are plus one and minus one.

628
00:36:36,881 --> 00:36:38,943
Every kind of particle picks one:

629
00:36:38,943 --> 00:36:44,256
symmetric wavefunctions for bosons, like photons, antisymmetric ones for fermions,

630
00:36:44,256 --> 00:36:45,656
like electrons.

631
00:36:45,656 --> 00:36:48,831
Which particles are which is the spin-statistics theorem:

632
00:36:48,831 --> 00:36:52,593
integer spin means boson, half-integer means fermion;

633
00:36:52,593 --> 00:36:54,793
its proof needs relativity.

634
00:36:54,793 --> 00:37:00,606
In a flat, two-dimensional world there's a third option, called anyons.

635
00:37:01,047 --> 00:37:02,285
Here's what that does.

636
00:37:02,285 --> 00:37:06,447
Two particles in a box, one in the lowest state and one in the second.

637
00:37:06,447 --> 00:37:09,735
If they were distinguishable, the wavefunction would be this.

638
00:37:09,735 --> 00:37:12,785
Symmetrize it, and it piles up along the diagonal:

639
00:37:12,785 --> 00:37:15,835
bosons are found close together more often.

640
00:37:15,835 --> 00:37:19,710
Antisymmetrize it, and it vanishes along the entire diagonal:

641
00:37:19,710 --> 00:37:23,689
two identical fermions are never found at the same place.

642
00:37:23,689 --> 00:37:27,226
The chance of finding the two within a tenth of the box of each other:

643
00:37:27,226 --> 00:37:31,326
twenty percent if they're distinguishable, thirty-eight for bosons, under

644
00:37:31,326 --> 00:37:32,914
two for fermions.

645
00:37:32,914 --> 00:37:34,414
There's no force here.

646
00:37:34,414 --> 00:37:37,676
The Hamiltonian is the same in all three cases;

647
00:37:37,676 --> 00:37:42,214
this is a correlation produced by symmetry alone.

648
00:37:42,622 --> 00:37:47,197
Put two fermions in the same state, and the antisymmetric combination is zero:

649
00:37:47,197 --> 00:37:48,685
there's no such state.

650
00:37:48,685 --> 00:37:52,585
That's Pauli's exclusion principle, from 1925.

651
00:37:52,585 --> 00:37:57,147
For N fermions, the antisymmetric state is a determinant of their single-particle

652
00:37:57,147 --> 00:38:01,585
wavefunctions, and a determinant with two equal rows vanishes.

653
00:38:01,585 --> 00:38:05,235
Hold one fermion still, and the others are kept away from it:

654
00:38:05,235 --> 00:38:09,072
a hole travels with every electron.

655
00:38:09,539 --> 00:38:13,576
Bosons do the opposite, and the most striking demonstration uses light.

656
00:38:13,576 --> 00:38:18,251
Send two identical photons into a half-silvered mirror, one from each side.

657
00:38:18,251 --> 00:38:22,764
Each photon is either transmitted, with amplitude one over root two, or reflected,

658
00:38:22,764 --> 00:38:24,964
with amplitude i over root two.

659
00:38:24,964 --> 00:38:28,839
For the photons to leave by different ports, both must be transmitted, or

660
00:38:28,839 --> 00:38:30,251
both reflected.

661
00:38:30,251 --> 00:38:33,189
Those two amplitudes are one half and minus one half:

662
00:38:33,189 --> 00:38:34,864
they cancel exactly.

663
00:38:34,864 --> 00:38:38,564
The photons always leave together.

664
00:38:39,039 --> 00:38:44,026
Delay one photon so they no longer overlap, and they act independently, splitting

665
00:38:44,026 --> 00:38:45,576
up half the time.

666
00:38:45,576 --> 00:38:49,364
As the delay goes to zero, coincidences vanish.

667
00:38:49,364 --> 00:38:54,751
This dip was measured by Hong, Ou and Mandel in 1987, and it's now a standard

668
00:38:54,751 --> 00:38:57,864
test of whether two photons are truly identical.

669
00:38:59,911 --> 00:39:04,324
Helium has two electrons, and the term that couples them, their repulsion,

670
00:39:04,324 --> 00:39:08,736
one over r one two, makes it impossible to solve exactly.

671
00:39:08,736 --> 00:39:13,099
Ignore that term, and each electron sits in a hydrogen-like orbit around a

672
00:39:13,099 --> 00:39:14,811
nucleus of charge two:

673
00:39:14,811 --> 00:39:18,674
an energy of minus 108.8 electron volts.

674
00:39:18,674 --> 00:39:21,261
The measured value is minus 79.0.

675
00:39:21,261 --> 00:39:24,186
The repulsion matters.

676
00:39:24,611 --> 00:39:26,949
First-order perturbation theory says:

677
00:39:26,949 --> 00:39:29,924
average the repulsion over the unperturbed state.

678
00:39:29,924 --> 00:39:34,674
Each electron is a spherical cloud, and by Newton's shell theorem, a spherical

679
00:39:34,674 --> 00:39:38,724
shell of charge acts like a point charge at its center from outside, and like

680
00:39:38,724 --> 00:39:40,786
nothing at all from inside.

681
00:39:40,786 --> 00:39:44,899
That reduces a six-dimensional integral to a two-dimensional one, and the

682
00:39:44,899 --> 00:39:48,824
answer is exactly five eighths of Z, in atomic units:

683
00:39:48,824 --> 00:39:51,236
34 electron volts.

684
00:39:51,236 --> 00:39:54,124
So the estimate becomes minus 74.8:

685
00:39:54,124 --> 00:39:57,636
much better, but now too high.

686
00:39:58,053 --> 00:40:00,766
We can do better with the variational principle.

687
00:40:00,766 --> 00:40:04,016
Expand any trial state in the true eigenstates:

688
00:40:04,016 --> 00:40:08,303
its average energy is a weighted average of the eigenvalues, so it can never

689
00:40:08,303 --> 00:40:10,241
be below the lowest one.

690
00:40:10,241 --> 00:40:14,578
Every guess gives an upper bound, and the best guess in a family is the one

691
00:40:14,578 --> 00:40:16,503
with the lowest energy.

692
00:40:16,503 --> 00:40:20,928
Let each electron see an effective charge zeta instead of two, because each

693
00:40:20,928 --> 00:40:24,428
electron partly screens the nucleus from the other.

694
00:40:24,428 --> 00:40:29,478
The energy is a parabola in zeta, with its minimum at twenty-seven sixteenths,

695
00:40:29,478 --> 00:40:33,620
giving minus 77.5 electron volts.

696
00:40:33,620 --> 00:40:38,595
A computer solution of the full two-electron equation, keeping only the spherically

697
00:40:38,595 --> 00:40:43,220
symmetric part of the repulsion, gets to minus 78.3.

698
00:40:43,220 --> 00:40:49,395
With everything included, theory and experiment agree at minus 79.0.

699
00:40:49,895 --> 00:40:53,782
Now the excited state with one electron in the one S orbital and one in the

700
00:40:53,782 --> 00:40:54,282
two S.

701
00:40:54,282 --> 00:40:58,145
Here the two electrons can have opposite spins or parallel ones.

702
00:40:58,145 --> 00:41:03,095
The total wavefunction must be antisymmetric, so parallel spins force an antisymmetric

703
00:41:03,095 --> 00:41:04,307
spatial part.

704
00:41:04,307 --> 00:41:08,732
Here are both states, computed on the plane of the two radii, r one and r

705
00:41:08,732 --> 00:41:09,682
two.

706
00:41:09,682 --> 00:41:12,770
The triplet's wavefunction vanishes along the diagonal:

707
00:41:12,770 --> 00:41:17,520
the electrons keep apart, repel each other less, and have lower energy.

708
00:41:17,520 --> 00:41:21,470
The computed splitting is 0.82 electron volts;

709
00:41:21,470 --> 00:41:23,807
the measured one is 0.80.

710
00:41:23,807 --> 00:41:27,945
That's the origin of Hund's rule, and of magnetism in materials:

711
00:41:27,945 --> 00:41:34,070
an energy that depends on spin, although no magnetic force is involved.

712
00:41:34,486 --> 00:41:38,486
With more electrons, the exclusion principle forces them into higher and higher

713
00:41:38,486 --> 00:41:40,699
orbitals, filling shells.

714
00:41:40,699 --> 00:41:44,574
Here is the energy needed to remove the outermost electron, for every element

715
00:41:44,574 --> 00:41:47,486
up to radon, from NIST's measurements.

716
00:41:47,486 --> 00:41:51,311
It peaks at the noble gases, where a shell has just been completed, and plunges

717
00:41:51,311 --> 00:41:55,811
at the alkali metals, whose one extra electron starts a new shell, far out

718
00:41:55,811 --> 00:41:57,274
and well screened.

719
00:41:57,274 --> 00:42:01,436
The periodic table is the exclusion principle, written in chemistry.

720
00:42:03,476 --> 00:42:06,614
A solid is a lattice of atoms, each a potential well.

721
00:42:06,614 --> 00:42:08,664
Let's build one, well by well.

722
00:42:08,664 --> 00:42:10,401
One well has its own levels.

723
00:42:10,401 --> 00:42:13,426
Put a second well beside it, and each level splits in two:

724
00:42:13,426 --> 00:42:16,976
the particle can tunnel between the wells, and the even and odd combinations

725
00:42:16,976 --> 00:42:19,051
have slightly different energies.

726
00:42:19,051 --> 00:42:19,876
Three wells:

727
00:42:19,876 --> 00:42:21,664
each level becomes three.

728
00:42:21,664 --> 00:42:23,639
Eight, sixteen, thirty-two:

729
00:42:23,639 --> 00:42:27,976
each level becomes a band of closely spaced levels, with gaps in between where

730
00:42:27,976 --> 00:42:29,901
there are no states at all.

731
00:42:29,901 --> 00:42:33,626
The deepest band is the narrowest, because tunneling through the barriers

732
00:42:33,626 --> 00:42:36,276
is hardest there.

733
00:42:36,710 --> 00:42:40,410
For an infinite lattice, symmetry tells us what the states look like.

734
00:42:40,410 --> 00:42:44,060
The potential repeats with period a, so the Hamiltonian commutes with the

735
00:42:44,060 --> 00:42:46,172
translation by one period.

736
00:42:46,172 --> 00:42:50,410
They share eigenstates, and since the translation is unitary, its eigenvalue

737
00:42:50,410 --> 00:42:51,635
is a phase:

738
00:42:51,635 --> 00:42:54,585
shifting by a multiplies psi by e to the i k a.

739
00:42:54,585 --> 00:42:59,460
So every stationary state is a plane wave, e to the i k x, times a function

740
00:42:59,460 --> 00:43:01,322
with the period of the lattice.

741
00:43:01,322 --> 00:43:04,535
That's Bloch's theorem, from 1928.

742
00:43:04,535 --> 00:43:05,460
Here's one:

743
00:43:05,460 --> 00:43:09,760
the size repeats from cell to cell, and the color advances by a quarter turn

744
00:43:09,760 --> 00:43:12,010
per cell.

745
00:43:12,493 --> 00:43:14,656
Now we can find the bands exactly.

746
00:43:14,656 --> 00:43:18,606
Carry a solution across one cell with a two-by-two transfer matrix.

747
00:43:18,606 --> 00:43:22,843
Bloch's condition says its eigenvalues are e to the plus and minus i k a,

748
00:43:22,843 --> 00:43:25,143
so cos k a equals half its trace:

749
00:43:25,143 --> 00:43:30,168
an explicit function of the energy, worked out by Kronig and Penney in 1931.

750
00:43:30,168 --> 00:43:33,206
But a cosine lies between minus one and one.

751
00:43:33,206 --> 00:43:37,268
Wherever this function strays outside that strip, there's no real k:

752
00:43:37,268 --> 00:43:40,218
those energies are forbidden, the gaps.

753
00:43:40,218 --> 00:43:44,031
Plot energy against k, and the bands are smooth curves.

754
00:43:44,031 --> 00:43:48,418
The levels of a ring of eight wells, computed separately, sit exactly on them,

755
00:43:48,418 --> 00:43:52,243
at the eight allowed values of k.

756
00:43:52,726 --> 00:43:54,814
Now fill the bands with electrons.

757
00:43:54,814 --> 00:43:58,476
Each band holds two electrons per cell, one of each spin.

758
00:43:58,476 --> 00:44:02,176
With one electron per cell, a band is half full, and the electrons at the

759
00:44:02,176 --> 00:44:05,926
top of the filled states can move into empty ones with an arbitrarily small

760
00:44:05,926 --> 00:44:06,539
push:

761
00:44:06,539 --> 00:44:07,501
a metal.

762
00:44:07,501 --> 00:44:11,264
With two per cell, the band is full, and the nearest empty states are across

763
00:44:11,264 --> 00:44:11,901
a gap:

764
00:44:11,901 --> 00:44:13,114
an insulator.

765
00:44:13,114 --> 00:44:16,164
Alan Wilson worked this out in 1931.

766
00:44:16,164 --> 00:44:18,851
That's why copper conducts and diamond doesn't.

767
00:44:20,850 --> 00:44:21,600
Part 5:

768
00:44:21,600 --> 00:44:24,175
Open systems.

769
00:44:24,908 --> 00:44:27,796
Here are two very different kinds of uncertainty.

770
00:44:27,796 --> 00:44:31,371
A spin in the superposition up plus down, over root two:

771
00:44:31,371 --> 00:44:32,483
pointing along x.

772
00:44:32,483 --> 00:44:36,058
And a spin that's up or down depending on a coin toss.

773
00:44:36,058 --> 00:44:39,608
Measure either one along z, and you get up half the time.

774
00:44:39,608 --> 00:44:43,971
But measure along x, and the superposition gives plus every time, while the

775
00:44:43,971 --> 00:44:47,133
coin-flip spin is still fifty-fifty.

776
00:44:47,133 --> 00:44:51,158
A list of states with probabilities is not a superposition, and to describe

777
00:44:51,158 --> 00:44:52,883
it we need a new object:

778
00:44:52,883 --> 00:44:57,208
the density matrix, rho, the probability-weighted sum of projectors onto the

779
00:44:57,208 --> 00:44:58,296
states.

780
00:44:58,296 --> 00:45:02,946
The Born rule becomes the trace of rho times the projector for the outcome.

781
00:45:02,946 --> 00:45:07,983
The superposition's density matrix has off-diagonal terms, called coherences;

782
00:45:07,983 --> 00:45:11,133
the coin flip's has none.

783
00:45:11,575 --> 00:45:16,150
For a spin, every density matrix is one half, times one plus r dot sigma,

784
00:45:16,150 --> 00:45:18,562
with r a vector no longer than one.

785
00:45:18,562 --> 00:45:20,100
Pure states have length one:

786
00:45:20,100 --> 00:45:21,337
the Bloch sphere.

787
00:45:21,337 --> 00:45:22,950
Mixtures fill the inside:

788
00:45:22,950 --> 00:45:24,025
the Bloch ball.

789
00:45:24,025 --> 00:45:26,337
And different mixtures can give the same rho:

790
00:45:26,337 --> 00:45:30,787
a coin flip between up and down, or between plus x and minus x, both land

791
00:45:30,787 --> 00:45:34,112
at the center, and no measurement can ever tell them apart.

792
00:45:34,112 --> 00:45:38,500
The density matrix is everything there is to know.

793
00:45:38,966 --> 00:45:41,429
Mixed states don't only come from ignorance.

794
00:45:41,429 --> 00:45:43,316
Take two spins in the singlet:

795
00:45:43,316 --> 00:45:45,004
a pure state of the pair.

796
00:45:45,004 --> 00:45:48,479
Ask what Alice alone can measure, by tracing out Bob's spin:

797
00:45:48,479 --> 00:45:50,804
summing over his possible outcomes.

798
00:45:50,804 --> 00:45:54,629
The result is one half times the identity, the center of the ball, with the

799
00:45:54,629 --> 00:45:56,829
largest entropy a spin can have.

800
00:45:56,829 --> 00:45:58,641
The whole is perfectly definite;

801
00:45:58,641 --> 00:46:01,454
each part, on its own, is completely random.

802
00:46:01,454 --> 00:46:05,466
That's entanglement, seen from one side.

803
00:46:05,908 --> 00:46:09,421
And the density matrix closes a gap from the start of this video:

804
00:46:09,421 --> 00:46:10,946
why the Born rule?

805
00:46:10,946 --> 00:46:15,496
Suppose you assign a probability to every possible outcome of every measurement,

806
00:46:15,496 --> 00:46:19,796
such that for any set of mutually perpendicular outcomes, the probabilities

807
00:46:19,796 --> 00:46:21,271
add to one.

808
00:46:21,271 --> 00:46:26,696
In 1957 Andrew Gleason proved that in three or more dimensions, the only such

809
00:46:26,696 --> 00:46:31,083
assignments are the trace of rho times the projector, for some density matrix

810
00:46:31,083 --> 00:46:32,233
rho.

811
00:46:32,233 --> 00:46:37,083
Given the vector structure of quantum states, the Born rule is the only consistent

812
00:46:37,083 --> 00:46:39,133
way to get probabilities out of them.

813
00:46:41,073 --> 00:46:43,423
Why don't we see cats in superpositions?

814
00:46:43,423 --> 00:46:46,035
The answer starts with the density matrix.

815
00:46:46,035 --> 00:46:50,385
Take a qubit, a times zero plus b times one, and let it interact with its

816
00:46:50,385 --> 00:46:51,560
environment:

817
00:46:51,560 --> 00:46:54,173
a stray photon, an air molecule.

818
00:46:54,173 --> 00:46:58,260
If the environment ends up in a state that depends on the qubit, E zero or

819
00:46:58,260 --> 00:47:02,498
E one, the qubit and its environment are now entangled.

820
00:47:02,498 --> 00:47:06,923
Trace out the environment, and the qubit's density matrix keeps its diagonal,

821
00:47:06,923 --> 00:47:11,360
the probabilities, but its coherences are multiplied by the overlap of the

822
00:47:11,360 --> 00:47:13,373
two environment states.

823
00:47:13,373 --> 00:47:17,710
Once the environment has recorded the difference, the overlap is zero, and

824
00:47:17,710 --> 00:47:21,048
so are the coherences.

825
00:47:21,531 --> 00:47:25,681
A real environment has many parts, and each takes a slightly different record.

826
00:47:25,681 --> 00:47:29,544
The overlap is a product of many numbers, each a little less than one.

827
00:47:29,544 --> 00:47:31,044
Here's a computed example:

828
00:47:31,044 --> 00:47:34,206
one qubit, dephased by N environment spins.

829
00:47:34,206 --> 00:47:37,131
With one, the coherence oscillates and comes back.

830
00:47:37,131 --> 00:47:39,556
With five, it comes back in bursts.

831
00:47:39,556 --> 00:47:42,356
With twenty, it's gone and barely flickers.

832
00:47:42,356 --> 00:47:46,006
With two hundred, it decays and never comes back on any time scale we could

833
00:47:46,006 --> 00:47:47,306
wait for.

834
00:47:47,306 --> 00:47:50,844
On the Bloch ball, the state's arrow shrinks onto the axis:

835
00:47:50,844 --> 00:47:54,556
a superposition has become a mixture.

836
00:47:55,006 --> 00:47:58,769
For the double slit, the environment records which slit the electron went

837
00:47:58,769 --> 00:48:02,906
through, and the interference term is multiplied by the overlap of the two

838
00:48:02,906 --> 00:48:04,069
records.

839
00:48:04,069 --> 00:48:08,269
A perfect record erases the fringes completely, leaving the sum of the two

840
00:48:08,269 --> 00:48:09,869
single-slit patterns;

841
00:48:09,869 --> 00:48:12,606
a partial record leaves faded fringes.

842
00:48:12,606 --> 00:48:16,931
This is complementarity, made quantitative.

843
00:48:17,373 --> 00:48:22,085
Here's a Schrödinger cat state, two separated packets, as a Wigner function,

844
00:48:22,085 --> 00:48:24,960
losing its coherence to a scattering environment.

845
00:48:24,960 --> 00:48:29,085
Each scattered particle multiplies the density matrix by a factor that depends

846
00:48:29,085 --> 00:48:31,698
on how far apart the two positions are:

847
00:48:31,698 --> 00:48:36,273
the off-diagonal terms decay like e to the minus Lambda t times the separation

848
00:48:36,273 --> 00:48:37,335
squared.

849
00:48:37,335 --> 00:48:41,298
The interference fringes between the blobs fade, exactly at the predicted

850
00:48:41,298 --> 00:48:45,398
rate, while the blobs themselves survive.

851
00:48:45,814 --> 00:48:50,014
And because the rate grows with the square of the separation, big superpositions

852
00:48:50,014 --> 00:48:51,277
die fast.

853
00:48:51,277 --> 00:48:53,127
Estimates from the literature:

854
00:48:53,127 --> 00:48:58,064
a dust grain a hundredth of a millimeter across, in air, loses a superposition

855
00:48:58,064 --> 00:49:03,652
of two positions its own size apart in about ten to the minus thirty-one seconds.

856
00:49:03,652 --> 00:49:09,489
Even the cosmic microwave background alone would do it in about a second.

857
00:49:09,939 --> 00:49:12,064
That's why the world looks classical:

858
00:49:12,064 --> 00:49:16,739
the environment is constantly measuring positions, and only states that survive

859
00:49:16,739 --> 00:49:18,302
that are ever seen.

860
00:49:18,302 --> 00:49:23,252
Serge Haroche's group watched it happen, step by step, with photons in a cavity

861
00:49:23,252 --> 00:49:25,014
in 1996.

862
00:49:25,014 --> 00:49:29,539
But decoherence doesn't explain why one particular outcome occurs.

863
00:49:29,539 --> 00:49:34,139
The density matrix ends up looking like a list of possibilities with probabilities,

864
00:49:34,139 --> 00:49:37,389
yet the whole state is still one superposition;

865
00:49:37,389 --> 00:49:41,552
which outcome we see is the measurement problem, and the interpretations of

866
00:49:41,552 --> 00:49:44,539
quantum mechanics part ways exactly there.

867
00:49:46,546 --> 00:49:47,346
Part 6:

868
00:49:47,346 --> 00:49:49,846
Relativity.

869
00:49:50,571 --> 00:49:53,533
Everything so far has been non-relativistic.

870
00:49:53,533 --> 00:49:57,808
Relativity demands that energy and momentum be related by E squared equals

871
00:49:57,808 --> 00:50:01,658
p squared c squared plus m squared c to the fourth.

872
00:50:01,658 --> 00:50:05,646
The obvious move is to replace E and p by their operators.

873
00:50:05,646 --> 00:50:09,796
That gives the Klein-Gordon equation, but it's second order in time, so the

874
00:50:09,796 --> 00:50:13,846
wavefunction now no longer determines its own future, and the quantity it

875
00:50:13,846 --> 00:50:15,633
conserves can be negative:

876
00:50:15,633 --> 00:50:17,846
it can't be a probability.

877
00:50:17,846 --> 00:50:23,546
In 1928 Paul Dirac insisted on keeping the Schrödinger form, first order in

878
00:50:23,546 --> 00:50:28,921
time, which means a Hamiltonian that is linear in momentum.

879
00:50:29,396 --> 00:50:34,546
So write H as c times alpha dot p, plus beta m c squared, with four unknown

880
00:50:34,546 --> 00:50:35,796
coefficients.

881
00:50:35,796 --> 00:50:38,821
Square it, carefully keeping the order of the factors.

882
00:50:38,821 --> 00:50:43,033
For this to equal p squared c squared plus m squared c to the fourth, each

883
00:50:43,033 --> 00:50:47,233
alpha and beta must square to one, and every pair must anticommute:

884
00:50:47,233 --> 00:50:51,371
alpha i times alpha j equals minus alpha j times alpha i.

885
00:50:51,371 --> 00:50:53,246
No numbers behave like that.

886
00:50:53,246 --> 00:50:56,171
They have to be matrices.

887
00:50:56,604 --> 00:51:01,017
The smallest matrices that work are four by four, built from the Pauli matrices

888
00:51:01,017 --> 00:51:02,229
of Part 1.

889
00:51:02,229 --> 00:51:04,129
Two by two is too small:

890
00:51:04,129 --> 00:51:08,017
only three two-by-two matrices anticommute, and we need four.

891
00:51:08,017 --> 00:51:10,579
So the wavefunction has four components.

892
00:51:10,579 --> 00:51:12,779
Two of them are spin up and spin down:

893
00:51:12,779 --> 00:51:15,617
spin one half appears without being put in.

894
00:51:15,617 --> 00:51:17,579
The doubling comes from something new:

895
00:51:17,579 --> 00:51:21,204
solutions with negative energy.

896
00:51:21,613 --> 00:51:23,263
The energies come in pairs:

897
00:51:23,263 --> 00:51:27,050
plus and minus the square root of p squared c squared plus m squared c to

898
00:51:27,050 --> 00:51:31,300
the fourth, two branches separated by a gap of two m c squared.

899
00:51:31,300 --> 00:51:33,425
The negative branch was a crisis.

900
00:51:33,425 --> 00:51:37,363
Dirac proposed in 1930 that those states are all filled, so that a missing

901
00:51:37,363 --> 00:51:40,975
one, a hole, would act like a particle of positive charge;

902
00:51:40,975 --> 00:51:44,900
a year later he predicted an anti-electron with the electron's mass.

903
00:51:44,900 --> 00:51:48,638
Carl Anderson found it in cosmic rays in 1932:

904
00:51:48,638 --> 00:51:50,213
the positron.

905
00:51:50,213 --> 00:51:54,663
Today the negative-energy solutions are understood through quantum field theory,

906
00:51:54,663 --> 00:51:58,038
as describing antiparticles.

907
00:51:58,496 --> 00:52:01,508
Mixing the two branches has a strange consequence.

908
00:52:01,508 --> 00:52:05,846
Here's a packet in a one-dimensional version of the Dirac equation, half positive

909
00:52:05,846 --> 00:52:08,996
energy and half negative, solved exactly.

910
00:52:08,996 --> 00:52:10,758
Its center doesn't sit still:

911
00:52:10,758 --> 00:52:15,758
it trembles, at a frequency of about two m c squared over h-bar, around the

912
00:52:15,758 --> 00:52:19,408
center of its positive-energy part, which doesn't move at all.

913
00:52:19,408 --> 00:52:23,246
Schrödinger called this Zitterbewegung, trembling motion.

914
00:52:23,246 --> 00:52:25,583
It isn't a point particle jittering;

915
00:52:25,583 --> 00:52:29,671
it's the interference between the two energy branches, beating at their energy

916
00:52:29,671 --> 00:52:30,733
difference.

917
00:52:30,733 --> 00:52:34,996
For a free electron it would be far too small and fast to see, but it has

918
00:52:34,996 --> 00:52:37,146
been simulated with trapped ions.

919
00:52:39,102 --> 00:52:42,352
Dirac's equation predicts more than antimatter.

920
00:52:42,352 --> 00:52:46,365
At low speeds, its upper two components obey a Schrödinger equation with a

921
00:52:46,365 --> 00:52:47,377
twist:

922
00:52:47,377 --> 00:52:52,865
the kinetic energy appears as sigma dot pi, squared, over 2m, where pi is

923
00:52:52,865 --> 00:52:54,077
p minus q A.

924
00:52:54,077 --> 00:52:56,852
The Pauli matrices obey this identity:

925
00:52:56,852 --> 00:53:01,527
sigma dot a times sigma dot b is a dot b plus i sigma dot a cross b.

926
00:53:01,527 --> 00:53:05,815
And because the components of pi don't commute in a magnetic field, pi cross

927
00:53:05,815 --> 00:53:07,627
pi isn't zero:

928
00:53:07,627 --> 00:53:09,202
it's i q h-bar B.

929
00:53:09,202 --> 00:53:13,640
So the kinetic energy contains a magnetic term, and it says the electron's

930
00:53:13,640 --> 00:53:16,640
spin is a magnet with g equal to two:

931
00:53:16,640 --> 00:53:22,552
twice as strong, for its angular momentum, as an orbiting charge.

932
00:53:23,052 --> 00:53:25,427
Measured, g is not exactly two.

933
00:53:25,427 --> 00:53:32,277
The best value, from a single electron held in a trap, is 2.00231930436, to

934
00:53:32,277 --> 00:53:33,702
thirteen digits.

935
00:53:33,702 --> 00:53:38,190
The small excess comes from the next layer of the theory, quantum electrodynamics:

936
00:53:38,190 --> 00:53:43,002
its first term, computed by Julian Schwinger in 1948, is the fine-structure

937
00:53:43,002 --> 00:53:44,902
constant over two pi.

938
00:53:44,902 --> 00:53:49,127
With the higher terms included, theory and experiment agree to about one part

939
00:53:49,127 --> 00:53:51,527
in a trillion.

940
00:53:51,994 --> 00:53:56,144
Dirac's equation can be solved exactly for hydrogen, and the energies depend

941
00:53:56,144 --> 00:54:00,906
not just on n but on j, the total angular momentum including spin.

942
00:54:00,906 --> 00:54:02,656
Zoom in on the second level.

943
00:54:02,656 --> 00:54:07,631
In Schrödinger's theory it's a single energy, minus 3.4 electron volts.

944
00:54:07,631 --> 00:54:09,494
In Dirac's, it splits:

945
00:54:09,494 --> 00:54:14,756
the 2 P three-halves states sit higher by 10.94 gigahertz, about forty-five

946
00:54:14,756 --> 00:54:18,244
millionths of an electron volt, within a quarter of a percent of the measured

947
00:54:18,244 --> 00:54:19,494
splitting.

948
00:54:19,494 --> 00:54:24,381
But Dirac's theory leaves 2 S one-half and 2 P one-half exactly together.

949
00:54:24,381 --> 00:54:29,744
In 1947 Willis Lamb and Robert Retherford found them apart by about a thousand

950
00:54:29,744 --> 00:54:33,844
megahertz, now measured as 1057.8.

951
00:54:33,844 --> 00:54:38,119
Explaining that shift, the electron interacting with fluctuations of the field

952
00:54:38,119 --> 00:54:42,894
itself, launched quantum electrodynamics.

953
00:54:43,361 --> 00:54:47,311
Each layer of the theory contains the one before it, and each new decimal

954
00:54:47,311 --> 00:54:49,023
place has been checked:

955
00:54:49,023 --> 00:54:54,173
Schrödinger's equation, Dirac's, and quantum electrodynamics, the most precisely

956
00:54:54,173 --> 00:54:55,786
tested theory in science.

957
00:54:57,959 --> 00:54:59,159
Let's look back.

958
00:54:59,159 --> 00:55:02,022
The rules that Part 1 guessed came out of symmetry:

959
00:55:02,022 --> 00:55:06,197
time gave the Schrödinger equation, space gave the commutator, boosts gave

960
00:55:06,197 --> 00:55:12,184
the Hamiltonian, rotations allowed spin, and local phase demanded electromagnetism.

961
00:55:12,184 --> 00:55:16,159
Feynman's sum over paths gave the same equation, and in the limit of small

962
00:55:16,159 --> 00:55:20,797
h-bar, Newton's laws, the old quantum rules and alpha decay.

963
00:55:20,797 --> 00:55:25,459
Perturbation theory and the golden rule turned it into numbers for real atoms.

964
00:55:25,459 --> 00:55:29,684
Exchange symmetry built the periodic table and the bands of solids.

965
00:55:29,684 --> 00:55:33,484
Density matrices gave us the Born rule and decoherence.

966
00:55:33,484 --> 00:55:40,959
And relativity, through Dirac, gave spin's magnetism, fine structure and antimatter.

967
00:55:41,376 --> 00:55:43,588
And one idea kept coming back:

968
00:55:43,588 --> 00:55:46,613
a phase is an area divided by h-bar.

969
00:55:46,613 --> 00:55:51,076
The area of a rectangle in phase space, when translations and boosts fail

970
00:55:51,076 --> 00:55:52,001
to commute;

971
00:55:52,001 --> 00:55:55,988
the magnetic flux through a loop, in the Aharonov-Bohm effect;

972
00:55:55,988 --> 00:56:00,901
and the area of a classical orbit, in the quantum condition.

973
00:56:01,334 --> 00:56:06,222
As in Part 1, every picture you've seen came from solving equations, not from

974
00:56:06,222 --> 00:56:07,934
an artist's impression:

975
00:56:07,934 --> 00:56:12,709
the electron going around a flux tube, the arrows of a thrown ball's paths,

976
00:56:12,709 --> 00:56:17,272
an orbit in phase space, the two electrons of helium keeping apart, and a

977
00:56:17,272 --> 00:56:21,109
cat state about to lose its fringes.

978
00:56:21,593 --> 00:56:25,855
From here, the roads lead to quantum field theory, where particles are excitations

979
00:56:25,855 --> 00:56:29,518
of fields and the vacuum itself shifts atomic levels;

980
00:56:29,518 --> 00:56:33,043
to quantum information, where entanglement is a resource;

981
00:56:33,043 --> 00:56:35,480
to the measurement problem, still open;

982
00:56:35,480 --> 00:56:39,068
and to gauge theories, where the same local-symmetry argument that gave us

983
00:56:39,068 --> 00:56:42,768
electromagnetism gives the other forces of nature.

984
00:56:42,768 --> 00:56:43,993
Thanks for watching.
